Feature: Data Extraction from sample_users_data Table

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the catalog is "agilisium_playground"
    And the table is "sample_users_data"

  Scenario: Successful data extraction for valid records
    Given the table "sample_users_data" exists in the schema "purgo_playground"
    When I query the table for records where "valid" is 1
    Then I should receive a dataset with columns "country_cd", "product_id", "qty_sold", "sales_date", "valid"
    And the "valid" column should only contain the value 1

  Scenario: Error when accessing non-existent table
    Given the table "non_existent_table" does not exist in the schema "purgo_playground"
    When I attempt to query the table
    Then I should receive an error message "Table 'non_existent_table' not found in schema 'purgo_playground'"

  Scenario Outline: Data validation for extracted records
    Given the table "sample_users_data" is queried for valid records
    When the data is extracted
    Then each record should have a "country_cd" in the format of two uppercase letters
    And each "product_id" should start with 'P' followed by four digits
    And "qty_sold" should be a positive integer
    And "sales_date" should be in the format YYYY-MM-DD
    Examples:
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date  | valid |
      | US         | P1001      | 50       | 2024-01-15  | 1     |
      | CA         | P1003      | 25       | 2024-01-17  | 1     |

  Scenario: Error when invalid data format is detected
    Given the table "sample_users_data" is queried for valid records
    When a record with "country_cd" not in the format of two uppercase letters is found
    Then I should receive an error message "Invalid country code format detected"

  Scenario: Error when invalid product_id format is detected
    Given the table "sample_users_data" is queried for valid records
    When a record with "product_id" not starting with 'P' followed by four digits is found
    Then I should receive an error message "Invalid product ID format detected"

  Scenario: Error when negative qty_sold is detected
    Given the table "sample_users_data" is queried for valid records
    When a record with "qty_sold" less than 0 is found
    Then I should receive an error message "Quantity sold cannot be negative"

  Scenario: Error when invalid sales_date format is detected
    Given the table "sample_users_data" is queried for valid records
    When a record with "sales_date" not in the format YYYY-MM-DD is found
    Then I should receive an error message "Invalid sales date format detected"